# Canonical components

Search these before building anything new. Reference implementations live in
`design-system/` (product-ready) and `design-lab/` (visual reference to port).

| Component | Role | Reference |
|---|---|---|
| `PlayUpMark` | Monogram, all sizes | `design-system/PlayUpMark.tsx` |
| Wordmark | Brand name + arrow in chrome | `design-lab/LabWordmark.tsx` |
| `PanelHead` | Panel title + optional neutral icon + right meta | `design-lab/LabShared.tsx` |
| `MatchRow` | One match, state-driven (score / time / pill / live) | `design-lab/LabShared.tsx` |
| Match Hero | Match object header, 3 states (scheduled/live/finished) | `design-lab/LabMatchSheet.tsx` |
| `Crest` | Team initials block | `design-lab/LabShared.tsx` |
| Trend icon | Slanted up/down/flat arrows | `design-lab/LabWordmark.tsx` |
| Status pill | `ds-status` tones (success/attention/error/info/neutral) | design system CSS |
| Buttons | `ds-btn--primary/secondary/ghost` — one primary per surface | design system CSS |
| Dialog / Drawer | Overlay level | existing shell components |
| Attention row | Count + icon + label + action (D9 recipe) | `design-lab/LabCockpit.tsx` |
| Cycle line | Lifecycle progress (Préparation → … → Terminée) | `design-lab/LabCockpit.tsx` |

## Rules

- A new component must have a **visual or behavioral reason to exist** —
  technical reusability alone does not justify one.
- Never re-style a canonical component locally (no inline overrides of
  scores, pills, buttons).
- State-driven rendering: normal state implicit, notable states explicit
  (MatchRow is the model).
